Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work solely
                      through Official Factories and Covered Descendants,
                      including calling their functions to create, configure,
                      administer, and use Covered Descendants, and using the
                      interfaces to integrate with those deployments.

                      An "Official Factory" is an original, unmodified Chainwall
                      factory deployed by OKcontract Pte. Ltd. and identified
                      by chain ID and contract address in deployment records
                      published by OKcontract Pte. Ltd.

                      A "Covered Descendant" is a contract created directly or
                      indirectly through an Official Factory's intended creation
                      functions, including its configured component deployers
                      and descendant factories, whose Chainwall code consists
                      solely of original, unmodified implementations supplied
                      by OKcontract Pte. Ltd. for that deployment. This includes
                      the use of those implementations by its proxies and
                      clones. A replacement implementation or facet qualifies
                      only if supplied by OKcontract Pte. Ltd. and expressly
                      designated by it for use with that deployment.

                      Ordinary configuration, ownership transfers, policy and
                      membership changes, and other state changes through the
                      intended interfaces do not by themselves modify the code
                      for purposes of this grant. Calling a factory to create a
                      contract through its intended creation functions is
                      covered even when the caller is a third party.

                      This grant does not permit production use of independently
                      deployed copies, even with identical bytecode, or of
                      modified or forked Chainwall implementations. Connecting
                      such a deployment to an Official Factory or a Covered
                      Descendant does not make it a Covered Descendant.

